use overlays in conjunction with pointers to functions, which sort of makes
sense since if a new overlay get swapped in, the pointer to the previous
overlay function will point to garbage.  This is why trying just to overlay
zap.c fails miserably (there's function pointers used in zap.c).  Can a code
guru please tell me which, if any, functions are completely untouched by
function pointers and hense would be safe to overlay?
